KANA=Kana
CREDITS=Stroke order from KanjiVG (Ulrich Apel); readings, meanings and example words from KANJIDIC2 and JMdict (EDRDG); example sentences from Tatoeba (tatoeba.org, CC BY 2.0 FR); JLPT levels from Jonathan Waller’s lists. Handwriting and text recognition by Google ML Kit, which sends Google anonymous usage data while it is on. Every licence in full: Licences.
WELCOME=Welcome
WELCOME_SKIP=Skip
WELCOME_START=Start writing
WELCOME_1_TITLE=Welcome to Kana
WELCOME_1=Write Japanese by hand, the way it is written: Kana shows every character’s strokes in order, reads what you write and tells you how well it went. It works offline, and everything stays on this device.
WELCOME_2_TITLE=Pencil or finger
WELCOME_2=Write with the Apple Pencil — fingers then move the page — or, with the hand on the bar, with one finger, and move the page with two. Kana switches by itself when the Pencil writes. The tools are on a bar you can drag anywhere; a double tap on its handle folds it away.
WELCOME_3_TITLE=Long press, and the lasso
WELCOME_3=Press and hold on the page for its menu: paste, paste text written as handwriting, text from a photo or the camera. Draw around writing with the lasso to copy it, copy it as text, translate it or check it.
WELCOME_4_TITLE=Learn
WELCOME_4=The menu at the top left has everything to study: kanji and kana with their stroke order, words to read and listen to, practice, reviews, exams, your album and statistics — and Settings, where your data is.

